<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<!--
  vibeos.Installer1: App Installer's interface for other apps (Software first), on the session bus.

  Bus name vibeos.Installer, object /vibeos/Installer. App Installer is D-Bus activatable: the first call starts it,
  and it stays while it has jobs.

  An app asks for an install or an uninstall and gets a job id back at once. App Installer then does the whole job
  by the same rules as when a person opens a .deb file in it: it looks the package up (refreshing the package lists
  first when they are old), lets PackageKit check what else would change, and asks the user to confirm when there
  is something to confirm. Then PackageKit does it, and polkit asks for the password (the shell's dialog). The caller
  never sees a password and decides nothing: it follows the job through Progress and Finished.

  App Installer asks (a bottom sheet over the caller's window, see "parent-window") before:
    - replacing an installed version with a newer one, an older one (a downgrade), or the same one again;
    - installing or removing other packages along with the one asked for;
    - any uninstall;
    - installing any .deb file (InstallFile).
  A new package with nothing else to install goes straight to polkit's password dialog. App Installer refuses,
  without asking, to remove part of VibeOS (any vibeos-* package), the shell, the window manager or the session, or a
  package the system marks Essential or Priority: required, or to install something that would remove one; the job
  then finishes as "refused".

  No other window of App Installer's opens for a job asked for here: the caller shows the progress.

  Options (a{sv}) for InstallPackage, InstallFile and RemovePackage:
    "parent-window"  s   the caller's window, as an xdg-foreign handle: "wayland:" and the handle
                         gdk_wayland_toplevel_export_handle (GTK 4) gives. App Installer's sheet is made transient
                         for it. Without it the sheet is a window of its own.

  Status, in Progress (what the job is doing now):
    "reading"           reading the file, or looking the package up
    "refreshing"        refreshing the package lists (when they are more than six hours old)
    "checking"          PackageKit's dry run: what else it installs or removes
    "asking"            the sheet is up, waiting for the user's answer
    "starting"          the real transaction is starting
    "waiting-for-auth"  polkit is asking for the password
    "waiting-for-lock"  another install or update (apt, Software, unattended-upgrades) is running; it waits
    "downloading"
    "installing"
    "removing"
    "finishing"
    "stopping"          Cancel was called and PackageKit is stopping
  Percent is 0 to 100, or -1 when not known.

  Result, in Finished:
    "done"       installed or removed (or already installed in that version: nothing to do)
    "cancelled"  the user said no (in the sheet, or by closing the password dialog), or Cancel stopped it
    "refused"    App Installer will not do it, or it cannot be done: a dependency cannot be met, no such package,
                 it would remove part of VibeOS, it is made for another architecture
    "failed"     it went wrong: no network, another install holding the lock, a broken package, no space, ...
  Message is one sentence for the user, in English ("Notes 1.3 is installed.", "Packages it needs could not be
  downloaded. Check the internet connection and try again.").

  The signals are sent to the caller that asked for the job only (not broadcast): subscribe with sender
  vibeos.Installer and path /vibeos/Installer.
-->
<node>
  <interface name="vibeos.Installer1">
    <!-- Install the package `name` from the software sources (apt's), its newest version for this device. -->
    <method name="InstallPackage">
      <arg name="name" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="options" type="a{sv}" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="job" type="u" direction="out"/>
    </method>
    <!-- Install a .deb file, by its absolute path (a file the calling user can read). Always asks first. -->
    <method name="InstallFile">
      <arg name="path" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="options" type="a{sv}" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="job" type="u" direction="out"/>
    </method>
    <!-- Uninstall the installed package `name`, and the packages that depend on it (the sheet names them).
         Nothing else: what it pulled in when it was installed stays (no autoremove). -->
    <method name="RemovePackage">
      <arg name="name" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="options" type="a{sv}" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="job" type="u" direction="out"/>
    </method>
    <!-- Stop a job of the caller's own. Before the real transaction it always stops; during it, only while
         PackageKit can stop it (the download), not once dpkg runs. Finished follows. -->
    <method name="Cancel">
      <arg name="job" type="u" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <!-- Whether `name` is installed: "installed" (installed_version set; available_version is the newest in the
         software sources, or the installed one), "available" (not installed, in the software sources) or
         "not-installed" (neither). Answers from the package lists as they are: no refresh. -->
    <method name="GetState">
      <arg name="name" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="state" type="s" direction="out"/>
      <arg name="installed_version" type="s" direction="out"/>
      <arg name="available_version" type="s" direction="out"/>
    </method>
    <signal name="Progress">
      <arg name="job" type="u"/>
      <arg name="percent" type="i"/>
      <arg name="status" type="s"/>
    </signal>
    <signal name="Finished">
      <arg name="job" type="u"/>
      <arg name="result" type="s"/>
      <arg name="message" type="s"/>
    </signal>
  </interface>
</node>
